-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedules 1 to 5A: cases for the seat (layer 2). The questions are the exported rules of uc3-seat.l4.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (a plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98.
--
-- EVERY EXPECTED VALUE IS WRITTEN HERE FROM THE TEXT, beside the case, before the file was run: none was copied from what the seat printed. The comment above each case names the
-- provision that gives the expected value. Every question has at least one case that answers it positively and one that does not where the answer has two outcomes.
-- An input that a case does not mention is FALSE, 0, England, "a single claimant", "monthly payments", "neither received nor so entitled" or, for a date, 1 January 2025.
-- The cases that rest on a reading the text does not settle name the fork in NOTES.md (U3-F8 counting months, U3-F20 what applies after the 12 months of Schedule 3 paragraph 6).
-- Each call gives its arguments in the order of the question's GIVEN lines in uc3-seat.l4; the second comment line above a call lists the inputs that differ from the defaults, by name. Amounts are in pounds.

-- A size category of accommodation as a number, so that an assertion can state it: 0 for shared accommodation (no size category has no bedroom), otherwise the number of bedrooms.
GIVEN category IS A `Category of accommodation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`uc3 case — the number of bedrooms in a category of accommodation` category MEANS
    CONSIDER category
    WHEN `shared accommodation` THEN 0
    WHEN `accommodation of a size given by a number of bedrooms` n THEN n

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element (Sch 1 paras 2, 3, 3A, 3B)?
-- Sch 1 para 2(a): a payment of rent is a rent payment, and nothing in paragraph 3 excludes it.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is rent = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 1 para 2(b): a payment for a licence to occupy is a rent payment.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is for a licence = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element` England FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 1 para 2: a payment that is none of the listed kinds is not a rent payment.
-- Inputs: all at their defaults.
#ASSERT `Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 1 para 3(a): ground rent is excluded.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is rent = TRUE; what I pay is ground rent = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 1 para 3(b): payments in respect of a tent are excluded.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is rent = TRUE; my home is a tent = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 1 para 3(d): payments in respect of a care home are excluded.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is rent = TRUE; my home is a care home = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 1 para 3(g) with 7(2): a payment that is in part for services or facilities is a service charge payment, and so is not a rent payment.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is rent = TRUE; what I pay is partly for services or facilities = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 1 para 3(h) with 3A(2): exempt accommodation is specified accommodation, so the payment is not a rent payment.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is rent = TRUE; my home is exempt accommodation = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 1 para 3(i) with 3B(2) (Case 1): rent payable to a local authority for accommodation it makes available to discharge its homelessness functions, not exempt accommodation, is temporary accommodation.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is rent = TRUE; my landlord is a local authority = TRUE; my home is made available for homeless people under a duty of the local authority = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 1 para 2(e)(i): a resident's contribution to almshouses provided by a housing association that is a registered charity is a rent payment.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is an almshouse contribution = TRUE; the almshouses are provided by a housing association = TRUE; that housing association is a registered charity = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 1 para 2(e): the housing association is neither a registered charity nor an exempt charity, so the contribution is not within paragraph 2.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is an almshouse contribution = TRUE; the almshouses are provided by a housing association = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Is what I pay a service charge payment for the housing costs element (Sch 1 paras 7, 8)?
-- Sch 1 para 7(2)(a): a payment in part for services or facilities is a service charge payment; paragraph 8 is not engaged because the calculation is not under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or Schedule 5.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is partly for services or facilities = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Is what I pay a service charge payment for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 1 para 7(2): a payment that is not for services or facilities (even in part) is not a service charge payment.
-- Inputs: all at their defaults.
#ASSERT `Is what I pay a service charge payment for the housing costs element` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 1 para 7(3)(a): a payment for which a qualifying loan was taken out is excluded.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is partly for services or facilities = TRUE; a mortgage interest loan was taken out for what I pay = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Is what I pay a service charge payment for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 1 para 7(3)(b)(iii): services for a person occupying a care home are excluded.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is partly for services or facilities = TRUE; my home is a care home = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Is what I pay a service charge payment for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 1 para 7(1)(c): in a Part 5 or Schedule 5 case the payment must meet every paragraph 8 condition, and none is met here.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is partly for services or facilities = TRUE; my housing costs element is worked out under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or Schedule 5 = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Is what I pay a service charge payment for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 1 para 8(3) to (6): right-to-occupy condition met, category B (communal areas), reasonable amount and description, and none of the fourth condition's exclusions, so every condition is met.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is partly for services or facilities = TRUE; my housing costs element is worked out under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or Schedule 5 = TRUE; the right to occupy depends on making the payments = TRUE; the payments are for communal areas = TRUE; the costs are of a reasonable amount = TRUE; the services are of a reasonable description = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Is what I pay a service charge payment for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 1 para 8(6)(c): payments for food, medical or personal services fail the fourth condition.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: what I pay is partly for services or facilities = TRUE; my housing costs element is worked out under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or Schedule 5 = TRUE; the right to occupy depends on making the payments = TRUE; the payments are for communal areas = TRUE; the costs are of a reasonable amount = TRUE; the services are of a reasonable description = TRUE; the payments are for food or medical or personal services = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Is what I pay a service charge payment for the housing costs element` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Am I liable to make the payments, or treated as liable (Sch 2 paras 1 to 4)?
-- A claimant who is liable is liable.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I am liable in fact = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to make the payments or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` `rent payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE `a single claimant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Nobody is liable and no provision of Part 1 applies.
-- Inputs: all at their defaults.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to make the payments or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a single claimant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 2 para 1(1)(a): treated as liable where the person liable is a child or qualifying young person the claimant is responsible for.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the person who is liable is a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to make the payments or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` `rent payments` FALSE TRUE FALSE `a single claimant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 1(1)(b): a member of a couple claiming as a single person is treated as liable where the other member is liable.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the person who is liable is my partner = TRUE; my claim basis = `a single claimant who is a member of a couple`.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to make the payments or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE TRUE `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 1(2): sub-paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a person claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4).
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the person who is liable is my partner = TRUE; my claim basis = `a single claimant who is a member of a couple`; I am claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4) = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to make the payments or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE TRUE `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 2 para 2: all four conditions are met.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the person who is liable is not making the payments = TRUE; I have to make the payments to stay in my home = TRUE; it would be unreasonable to expect me to make other arrangements = TRUE; it is otherwise reasonable to treat me as liable = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to make the payments or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a single claimant` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 2: the fourth condition (otherwise reasonable) is not met, so the claimant is not treated as liable.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the person who is liable is not making the payments = TRUE; I have to make the payments to stay in my home = TRUE; it would be unreasonable to expect me to make other arrangements = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to make the payments or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a single claimant` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 2 para 3: waiver by way of reasonable compensation for repair works the person owed would otherwise have carried out.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the liability to make the payments has been waived = TRUE; the waiver is compensation for repair or re-decoration I carried out = TRUE; the works are works the landlord would otherwise have carried out = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to make the payments or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a single claimant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 4(1): treated as liable for the whole of a rent free period (rent payments).
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the arrangements provide for rent free periods = TRUE; this is a period in which I have no liability to make one or more of the payments = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to make the payments or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a single claimant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 4(1) names rent payments and service charge payments only, so owner-occupier payments are not covered.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the kind of payment = `owner-occupier payments`; the arrangements provide for rent free periods = TRUE; this is a period in which I have no liability to make one or more of the payments = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to make the payments or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` `owner-occupier payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a single claimant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Am I treated as not liable to make the payments (Sch 2 paras 5 to 8)?
-- Sch 2 para 5(1)(a): rent owed to the claimant's partner who lives in the accommodation.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the person I pay lives in my home = TRUE; the person I pay is my partner = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` `rent payments` TRUE TRUE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 5(1)(c)(i): rent owed to a close relative (a parent) who lives in the accommodation.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the person I pay lives in my home = TRUE; the person I pay is related to me as = `a parent`.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` `rent payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE `a parent` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 5(1): the close relative does not live in the accommodation.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the person I pay is related to me as = `a parent`.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `a parent` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 2 para 5(2): service charge payments follow only where the claimant is treated as not liable for rent payments to the same person, and that fact is not stated.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the person I pay lives in my home = TRUE; the person I pay is my partner = TRUE; the kind of payment = `service charge payments`.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` `service charge payments` TRUE TRUE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 2 para 5(2): treated as not liable for rent to the same person, so also for service charge payments.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the person I pay lives in my home = TRUE; the person I pay is my partner = TRUE; the kind of payment = `service charge payments`; I am treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` `service charge payments` TRUE TRUE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 6(1)(a): rent owed to a company of which the claimant is a director.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I am a director of the company I pay = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE TRUE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 6(3), (4)(a): holding at least 10% of the shares makes the claimant an owner of the company.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the percentage of the shares in the company held by me and associates = 10.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 10 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 6(4)(a): 9% is below the 10% threshold, and no other limb is stated.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the percentage of the shares in the company held by me and associates = 9.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 9 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 2 para 7(1)(a): rent owed to a trustee of a trust whose trustees or beneficiaries include the claimant.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the payments are owed to a trustee of a trust = TRUE; the trustees or beneficiaries include me = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 8(1): owner-occupier payments owed to a person who lives in the claimant's household.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the kind of payment = `owner-occupier payments`; the payments are owed to a person who lives in my household = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` `owner-occupier payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 8(3): no liability for rent or owner-occupier payments, and the service charge is owed to a person in the household.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the kind of payment = `service charge payments`; the payments are owed to a person who lives in my household = TRUE; there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` `service charge payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- None of paragraphs 5 to 8 applies.
-- Inputs: all at their defaults.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- What amount of an increase because of arrears am I treated as not liable for (Sch 2 para 9)?
-- Sch 2 para 9(1): the whole increase resulting from arrears is an amount for which the claimant is treated as not liable (no preceding provision applies).
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the amount of the increase in the sum payable that results from arrears or any other unpaid liability = 25.5.
#ASSERT `What amount of an increase because of arrears am I treated as not liable for` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 25.5 EQUALS 25.5
-- Sch 2 para 9(2): paragraph 9(1) does not apply where the claimant is treated as not liable under paragraph 5; so no amount is carved out by paragraph 9.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the amount of the increase in the sum payable that results from arrears or any other unpaid liability = 25.5; the person I pay lives in my home = TRUE; the person I pay is my partner = TRUE.
#ASSERT `What amount of an increase because of arrears am I treated as not liable for` `rent payments` TRUE TRUE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 25.5 EQUALS 0

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Am I treated as not liable because my liability was contrived (Sch 2 para 10)?
-- Sch 2 para 10(1): the Secretary of State is satisfied that the liability was contrived.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the Secretary of State is satisfied that my liability was contrived = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable because my liability was contrived` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 2 para 10(2): paragraph 10(1) does not apply where the claimant is treated as not liable under an earlier provision of the Part.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the Secretary of State is satisfied that my liability was contrived = TRUE; the person I pay lives in my home = TRUE; the person I pay is my partner = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable because my liability was contrived` `rent payments` TRUE TRUE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 2 para 10(1): no satisfaction of the Secretary of State.
-- Inputs: all at their defaults.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as not liable because my liability was contrived` `rent payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE `not a listed relation` `not a listed relation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Is the accommodation I normally live in treated as my home (Sch 3 para 1)?
-- Sch 3 para 1(1): the accommodation normally occupied as home, of one dwelling.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: this is the accommodation I normally occupy as my home = TRUE; the number of dwellings my accommodation comprises = 1.
#ASSERT `Is the accommodation I normally live in treated as my home` TRUE 1 EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 3 para 1(2): no claimant is treated as occupying accommodation that comprises more than one dwelling (subject to the later paragraphs).
-- Inputs other than the defaults: this is the accommodation I normally occupy as my home = TRUE; the number of dwellings my accommodation comprises = 2.
#ASSERT `Is the accommodation I normally live in treated as my home` TRUE 2 EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 3 para 1(1): not the accommodation normally occupied as home.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the number of dwellings my accommodation comprises = 1.
#ASSERT `Is the accommodation I normally live in treated as my home` FALSE 1 EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Is my croft land treated as part of my home (Sch 3 para 2)?
-- Sch 3 para 2(1): croft land used for the purposes of the accommodation is treated as included.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: this is the accommodation I normally occupy as my home = TRUE; my accommodation is on or pertains to a croft = TRUE; the croft land is used for the purposes of my accommodation = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Is my croft land treated as part of my home` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 3 para 2(1): the croft land is not used for the purposes of the accommodation.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: this is the accommodation I normally occupy as my home = TRUE; my accommodation is on or pertains to a croft = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Is my croft land treated as part of my home` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Which home am I treated as normally occupying while my home is being repaired (Sch 3 para 3)?
-- Sch 3 para 3(1): the conditions are met for the other accommodation only.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I have to move into other accommodation because of essential repairs to my home = TRUE; I intend to return to the home under repair = TRUE; I meet the payment and liability conditions for the other accommodation = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Which home am I treated as normally occupying while my home is being repaired` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the other accommodation`
-- Sch 3 para 3(1): the conditions are met for the accommodation under repair only.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I have to move into other accommodation because of essential repairs to my home = TRUE; I intend to return to the home under repair = TRUE; I meet the payment and liability conditions for the home under repair = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Which home am I treated as normally occupying while my home is being repaired` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the accommodation under repair`
-- Sch 3 para 3(2): the conditions are met for both, so the general rule applies.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I have to move into other accommodation because of essential repairs to my home = TRUE; I intend to return to the home under repair = TRUE; I meet the payment and liability conditions for the other accommodation = TRUE; I meet the payment and liability conditions for the home under repair = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Which home am I treated as normally occupying while my home is being repaired` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the general rule in paragraph 1 applies`
-- Sch 3 para 3(1)(a) and (b) are not met (no move for repairs, no intention to return), so the general rule applies.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I meet the payment and liability conditions for the other accommodation = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Which home am I treated as normally occupying while my home is being repaired` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the general rule in paragraph 1 applies`

