-- What is my cap rent (Sch 4 para 25)?
-- Sch 4 para 25(2): the local housing allowance for the area and category of accommodation.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the local housing allowance for my area and category of accommodation = 600.
#ASSERT `What is my cap rent` 600 FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `accommodation A` EQUALS 600
-- Sch 4 para 25(3), (4)(a): the allowances for A and B differ and a single calculation is made, so the amount for the dwelling with the lower one (B, 450) is used.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to me = TRUE; a single calculation is made for me under paragraph 17 = TRUE; the local housing allowance for my area and category of accommodation = 600; the local housing allowance for accommodation A = 500; the local housing allowance for accommodation B = 450; this is the first calculation = TRUE; the accommodation for which the allowance was lower when the calculation was first made = `accommodation B`.
#ASSERT `What is my cap rent` 600 TRUE 500 450 TRUE TRUE FALSE `accommodation B` EQUALS 450
-- Sch 4 para 25(4)(b): the amount continues to be determined by reference to the accommodation recorded as the one that was lower at the first calculation (A), for as long as paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to the same A and B.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to me = TRUE; a single calculation is made for me under paragraph 17 = TRUE; the local housing allowance for my area and category of accommodation = 600; the local housing allowance for accommodation A = 500; the local housing allowance for accommodation B = 450.
#ASSERT `What is my cap rent` 600 TRUE 500 450 TRUE FALSE FALSE `accommodation A` EQUALS 500
-- Sch 4 para 25(4)(c): on re-housing the amount is re-determined by reference to the dwelling for which it is now lower (A, 400).
-- Inputs other than the defaults: paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to me = TRUE; a single calculation is made for me under paragraph 17 = TRUE; the local housing allowance for my area and category of accommodation = 600; the local housing allowance for accommodation A = 400; the local housing allowance for accommodation B = 450; I have been re-housed in other accommodation since the amount was last determined = TRUE; the accommodation for which the allowance was lower when the calculation was first made = `accommodation B`.
#ASSERT `What is my cap rent` 600 TRUE 400 450 TRUE FALSE TRUE `accommodation B` EQUALS 400
-- Sch 4 para 25(3)(b): the allowances for A and B are the same, so paragraph (4) does not apply and (2) gives the allowance for the renter's area and category (600).
-- Inputs other than the defaults: paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to me = TRUE; a single calculation is made for me under paragraph 17 = TRUE; the local housing allowance for my area and category of accommodation = 600; the local housing allowance for accommodation A = 500; the local housing allowance for accommodation B = 500.
#ASSERT `What is my cap rent` 600 TRUE 500 500 TRUE FALSE FALSE `accommodation A` EQUALS 600

