-- Inputs other than the defaults: I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for these payments = TRUE; the number of listed persons liable for the payments = 1; the number of bedrooms in my home = 2; the number of bedrooms I am entitled to = 2; the amount of each rent payment = 500; the number of other persons liable for the payments = 1; the Secretary of State is satisfied that sharing the payments by number of people would be unreasonable = TRUE; the amount the Secretary of State considers appropriate = 300.
#ASSERT `What is my housing costs element if I rent from a social landlord` 500 `monthly payments` FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 `monthly payments` FALSE 0 0 TRUE FALSE 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2 1 1 TRUE 300 0 EQUALS 300

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Will a deduction be made because I have more bedrooms than I am entitled to (Sch 4 para 36)?
-- Sch 4 para 36(1): the accommodation has 3 bedrooms and the renter is entitled to 2.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the number of bedrooms in my home = 3; the number of bedrooms I am entitled to = 2.
#ASSERT `Will a deduction be made because I have more bedrooms than I am entitled to` 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2 EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 4 para 36(1): the bedrooms do not exceed the entitlement.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the number of bedrooms in my home = 2; the number of bedrooms I am entitled to = 2.
#ASSERT `Will a deduction be made because I have more bedrooms than I am entitled to` 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2 EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 4 para 36(5): no deduction where regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) applies.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the number of bedrooms in my home = 3; the number of bedrooms I am entitled to = 2; regulation 26(4) to (6) applies to me = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Will a deduction be made because I have more bedrooms than I am entitled to` 3 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2 EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 4 para 36(6)(a): domestic violence, the victim living elsewhere, and evidence of a sanctuary scheme property with the circumstances consistent and contact made.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the number of bedrooms in my home = 3; the number of bedrooms I am entitled to = 2; domestic violence has been inflicted or threatened against me or a member of my extended benefit unit = TRUE; the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened it = TRUE; I provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity that I live in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme = TRUE; the sanctuary scheme is operated by a provider of social housing = TRUE; the victim's circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened = TRUE; the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity about such an incident = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Will a deduction be made because I have more bedrooms than I am entitled to` 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 4 para 36(6)(a)(iii): without the evidence the exemption does not apply, so the deduction is made.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the number of bedrooms in my home = 3; the number of bedrooms I am entitled to = 2; domestic violence has been inflicted or threatened against me or a member of my extended benefit unit = TRUE; the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened it = TRUE; the sanctuary scheme is operated by a provider of social housing = TRUE; the victim's circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened = TRUE; the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity about such an incident = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Will a deduction be made because I have more bedrooms than I am entitled to` 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 4 para 36(6)(a)(ii): the exception where the person is a qualifying young person who is a dependant keeps sub-paragraph (ii) satisfied even though the victim lives at the same address.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the number of bedrooms in my home = 3; the number of bedrooms I am entitled to = 2; domestic violence has been inflicted or threatened against me or a member of my extended benefit unit = TRUE; I provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity that I live in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme = TRUE; the sanctuary scheme is operated by a provider of social housing = TRUE; the victim's circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened = TRUE; the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity about such an incident = TRUE; that person is a qualifying young person who is a dependant of a member of my extended benefit unit = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Will a deduction be made because I have more bedrooms than I am entitled to` 3 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 EQUALS FALSE

