-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Have I got past the qualifying period for the housing costs element as an owner-occupier (Sch 5 para 5)?
-- Sch 5 para 5(1), (2)(a): 9 consecutive qualifying assessment periods have ended before this one.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the number of assessment periods in a row, not counting this one, that count towards my qualifying period = 9.
#ASSERT `Have I got past the qualifying period for the housing costs element as an owner-occupier` `a new award` 9 0 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 5 para 5(2)(a): only 8 qualifying periods so far.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the number of assessment periods in a row, not counting this one, that count towards my qualifying period = 8.
#ASSERT `Have I got past the qualifying period for the housing costs element as an owner-occupier` `a new award` 8 0 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sch 5 para 6(2), 7(2): one credited or carried-forward period completes the 9.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the number of assessment periods in a row, not counting this one, that count towards my qualifying period = 8; the assessment periods credited under paragraph 6(2) or carried forward under paragraph 7(2) = 1.
#ASSERT `Have I got past the qualifying period for the housing costs element as an owner-occupier` `a new award` 8 1 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 5 para 5(2)(b): 9 consecutive periods in which the owner-occupier would otherwise qualify.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the number of assessment periods in a row, not counting this one, that count towards my qualifying period = 9; my qualifying period is for = `an award from which an amount calculated under this Schedule has ceased to be included`.
#ASSERT `Have I got past the qualifying period for the housing costs element as an owner-occupier` `an award from which an amount calculated under this Schedule has ceased to be included` 9 0 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 5 para 7(3): an amount was already included in the award that ended, so no qualifying period applies.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: paragraph 7(3) applies to me = TRUE.
#ASSERT `Have I got past the qualifying period for the housing costs element as an owner-occupier` `a new award` 0 0 TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sch 5 para 5(1): no qualifying period has been completed.
-- Inputs: all at their defaults.
#ASSERT `Have I got past the qualifying period for the housing costs element as an owner-occupier` `a new award` 0 0 FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- How many assessment periods do my days of jobseeker's allowance or employment and support allowance count as (Sch 5 para 6)?
-- Sch 5 para 6(2): 62 days in assessment periods of 31 days (1 to 31 January) are 2 assessment periods.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I was entitled to a jobseeker's allowance immediately before my award of universal credit began = TRUE; the period comprises only days on which I was receiving that benefit = TRUE; the period is treated as if it were the whole or part of one or more assessment periods = TRUE; the day of the month of the last day of my assessment period = 31; the number of days on which I received that benefit in the period = 62.
#ASSERT `How many assessment periods do my days of jobseeker's allowance or employment and support allowance count as` TRUE FALSE 62 TRUE TRUE 2025 1 1 2025 1 31 EQUALS 2
-- Sch 5 para 6(2): 31 days in a 31-day assessment period are one.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I was entitled to a jobseeker's allowance immediately before my award of universal credit began = TRUE; the period comprises only days on which I was receiving that benefit = TRUE; the period is treated as if it were the whole or part of one or more assessment periods = TRUE; the day of the month of the last day of my assessment period = 31; the number of days on which I received that benefit in the period = 31.
#ASSERT `How many assessment periods do my days of jobseeker's allowance or employment and support allowance count as` TRUE FALSE 31 TRUE TRUE 2025 1 1 2025 1 31 EQUALS 1
-- Sch 5 para 6(1): not entitled to either allowance immediately before the award began.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: the period comprises only days on which I was receiving that benefit = TRUE; the period is treated as if it were the whole or part of one or more assessment periods = TRUE; the day of the month of the last day of my assessment period = 31; the number of days on which I received that benefit in the period = 62.
#ASSERT `How many assessment periods do my days of jobseeker's allowance or employment and support allowance count as` FALSE FALSE 62 TRUE TRUE 2025 1 1 2025 1 31 EQUALS 0
-- Sch 5 para 6(2): the permission to treat the days as assessment periods is not used.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I was entitled to a jobseeker's allowance immediately before my award of universal credit began = TRUE; the period comprises only days on which I was receiving that benefit = TRUE; the day of the month of the last day of my assessment period = 31; the number of days on which I received that benefit in the period = 62.
#ASSERT `How many assessment periods do my days of jobseeker's allowance or employment and support allowance count as` TRUE FALSE 62 TRUE FALSE 2025 1 1 2025 1 31 EQUALS 0

