#ASSERT `How many assessment periods are carried forward to my further award after my partner and I stop being a couple` TRUE FALSE TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS 0

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- What is my housing costs element as an owner-occupier (Sch 5 paras 9 and 13)?
-- Sch 5 paras 9 and 13: the monthly amount of the one service charge taken into account.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge = TRUE; I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the second service charge = TRUE; the qualifying period has ended = TRUE; the amount of each first service charge payment = 50.
#ASSERT `What is my housing costs element as an owner-occupier` 50 `monthly payments` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE 0 `monthly payments` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 50
-- Sch 5 para 9: the sum of the monthly amounts of both service charge payments: 50 + 30.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge = TRUE; I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the second service charge = TRUE; the qualifying period has ended = TRUE; the amount of each first service charge payment = 50; the amount of each second service charge payment = 30.
#ASSERT `What is my housing costs element as an owner-occupier` 50 `monthly payments` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE 30 `monthly payments` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 80
-- Sch 5 para 8: no payment is taken into account until the qualifying period has ended.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge = TRUE; I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the second service charge = TRUE; the amount of each first service charge payment = 50.
#ASSERT `What is my housing costs element as an owner-occupier` 50 `monthly payments` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE 0 `monthly payments` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- Sch 5 para 8: a payment already brought into account is not counted again, so only the first.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge = TRUE; I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the second service charge = TRUE; the qualifying period has ended = TRUE; the amount of each first service charge payment = 50; the amount of each second service charge payment = 30; the second service charge has already been brought into account = TRUE.
#ASSERT `What is my housing costs element as an owner-occupier` 50 `monthly payments` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE 30 `monthly payments` FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS 50
-- Sch 5 para 13(3)(c): a three-monthly payment is multiplied by 4 and divided by 12: 300 x 4 / 12 = 100.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge = TRUE; I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the second service charge = TRUE; the qualifying period has ended = TRUE; the amount of each first service charge payment = 300; how often the first service charge falls due = `three-monthly payments`.
#ASSERT `What is my housing costs element as an owner-occupier` 300 `three-monthly payments` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE 0 `monthly payments` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 100
-- Sch 5 para 13(4): with service charge free periods, 600 x 10 / 12 = 500.
-- Inputs other than the defaults: I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge = TRUE; I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the second service charge = TRUE; the qualifying period has ended = TRUE; the amount of each first service charge payment = 600; my first service charge arrangements provide for free periods = TRUE; the total number of first service charge payments in the 12 month period = 10.
#ASSERT `What is my housing costs element as an owner-occupier` 600 `monthly payments` TRUE 10 TRUE FALSE 0 `monthly payments` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 500

